"[2609.33732] Strong $q$-log-convexity of the $d$-Hoggatt polynomials (https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.33732)\nciteturn6view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.33732\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 158\nL0: 【0†Search】 【1†Submit】 【2†Donate†info.arxiv.org】 【3†Log in】\nL1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · 【4†Advanced search】\nL5: \nL6: # Mathematics > Combinatorics\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 27 Sep 2026]\nL9: # Title:Strong $q$-log-convexity of the $d$-Hoggatt polynomials\nL10: \nL11: Authors:【5†Shane Chern】, 【6†Wenle Shi】\nL12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Strong $q$-log-convexity of the $d$-Hoggatt polynomials, by Shane Chern and 1 other authors\nL14: \nL15: 【7†View PDF】 【8†HTML (experimental)】\nL16: > Abstract:In this paper, three ($q$-)log-convexity or concavity properties related to the $d$-Hoggatt numbers are investigated. First, we show that the $d$-Hoggatt transformation preserves the log-convexity of a sequence. We then establish the strong $q$-log-concavity of a $q$-analog of $d$-Hoggatt numbers. Finally, we prove the core result of this work, namely, the sequence of $d$-Hoggatt polynomials is strongly $q$-log-convex, based on the theory of Schur functions.\nL17: Subjects:  | Combinatorics (math.CO)\nL18: MSC (Mathematical Subject Classification) classes:  | 05E05, 05A05, 05A20\nL19: Cite as:  | 【9†arXiv:2609.33732】 [math.CO]\nL20:    | (or 【10†arXiv:2609.33732v1】 [math.CO] for this version)\nL21:    | 【11†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2609.33732†doi.org】 arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL22: ## Submission history\nL23: \nL24: From: Shane Chern [【12†view email】]\nL25: [v1] Sun, 27 Sep 2026 16:35:21 UTC (22 KB)\nL26: \nL27: Full-text links:\nL28: \nL29: ## Access Paper:\nL30: \nL31: View a PDF of the paper titled Strong $q$-log-convexity of the $d$-Hoggatt polynomials, by Shane C