la, while the palindromicity is proved by an involution on rectangular standard Young tableaux. Our result confirms a conjecture of Cigler.\nL17: Subjects:  | Combinatorics (math.CO); Number Theory (math.NT)\nL18: MSC (Mathematical Subject Classification) classes:  | 05A19, 05A15, 05E05, 11B65\nL19: Cite as:  | 【9†arXiv:2606.26950】 [math.CO]\nL20:    | (or 【10†arXiv:2606.26950v1】 [math.CO] for this version)\nL21:    | 【11†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2606.26950†doi.org】 arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL22: ## Submission history\nL23: \nL24: From: Shane Chern [【12†view email】]\nL25: [v1] Thu, 25 Jun 2026 12:23:57 UTC (8 KB)\nL26: \nL27: Full-text links:\nL28: \nL29: ## Access Paper:\nL30: \nL31: View a PDF of the paper titled Proof of Cigler's conjecture on $q$-Hoggatt numbers, by Shane Chern and 1 other authors\nL32: \nL33:   * 【7†View PDF】\nL34:   * 【8†HTML (experimental)】\nL35:   * 【13†TeX Source】\nL36: \nL37: 【14†view license】\nL38: \nL39: ### Current browse context:\nL40: \nL41: math.CO\nL42: \nL43: 【15†< prev】   |   【16†next >】\nL44: \nL45: 【17†new】 | 【18†recent】 | 【19†2026-06】\nL46: \nL47: Change to browse by:\nL48: \nL49: 【20†math】\nL50: 【21†math.NT】\nL51: ### References & Citations\nL52: \nL53:   * 【22†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu】\nL54:   * 【23†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com】\nL55:   * 【24†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org】\nL56: \nL57: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL58: \nL59: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL60: \nL61: [Button: ×]\nL62: \nL63: loading...\nL64: \nL65: Data provided by:\nL66: \nL67: ### Bookmark\nL68: \nL69: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL70: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL71: \nL72: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL73: \nL74: Bibliographic Explorer (【25†What is the Explorer?†info.arxiv.org】)\nL75: \nL76: [Input] Connected Papers Toggle\nL77: \n"
